		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Réponse à&#160;:  Arrêter le service postgresql.service pour de bon]]></title>
		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=29922#p29922"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Je ne suis pas certain que ça fonctionne (et je trouve ce redémarrage automatique un peu surprenant) <br />mais personnellement j&#039;aurais tendance à voir plutôt par là:</p><p>(extrait de man pg_ctlcluster):</p><div class="quotebox"><blockquote><div><p>/etc/postgresql/cluster-version/cluster-name/start.conf<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;This configuration file controls the start/stop behavior of the<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;cluster. See section &quot;STARTUP CONTROL&quot; in pg_createcluster(8) for<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;details.</p></div></blockquote></div><p>et mettre provisoirement &quot;disabled&quot; dans le fichier, vu que (cf man pg_createcluster):</p><div class="quotebox"><blockquote><div><p>disabled<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;Neither the init script, pg_ctlcluster(1), nor postgresql@.service<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;are permitted to start/stop the cluster. Please be aware that this<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;will not stop the cluster owner from calling lower level tools to<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;control the postgres process; this option is only meant to prevent<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;accidents during maintenance, not more.</p></div></blockquote></div>]]></content>
